it's not well who flees from  the scene he gets killed by way more  Royce who has now risen as a white old  man Garrett is the one who survives this  attack I think the prologue does do a  great job at giving us readers extra  information that helps advance the  overall story we now know this will not  simply be just a game of Thrones between  the various houses of Westeros now we  know there is this supernatural  underlying threat that could jeopardize  life in the Seven Kingdoms as we know it  the White Walkers are back  and they made a great first impression  that shows they are a force to be  reckoned with the opening scene  essentially sets the tone for the entire  series which is one of the reasons why I  love it so much I think it was an  amazing way to open up a story or  television show for that matter if this  doesn't leave you wanting more then I  don't know what will obviously this is  only a small glimpse of what's to come  later now most of you should know I love  to make a lot of theories about how I  think things will end but I don't want  to start revealing any of that just yet  since this is only an introduction to  the series I will say this though my  theories for how the books end are very  different from what my theories were for  how the show ends for obvious reasons  like I said earlier I will start to get  into that stuff once I get to some of  the other chapters that helps back up  some of my ideas for the end game for  those of you who have not read the books  I hope the video gave you a good idea of  what happens at the beginning of the  game of Thrones book either way I really  hope you all watch the next video I want  to thank everyone for stopping by to  check out this first one I appreciate  that as always have a great day I will  see you very soon bye  [Music]  [Music]
 

